<title>AUSTRALIA: Macmin says to defer Sinivit gold project.</title>
<headline>Macmin says to defer Sinivit gold project.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Junior miner Macmin NL said on Tuesday it had decided to defer further mine development at Sinivit in Papua New Guinea due to the decline in the gold price.</p>
<p>Macmin said the project was uneconomic, or at best marginally economic, at a gold price of US$320 an ounce.</p>
<p>The deferment is subject to approval by the Papua New Guinea Department of Mining and Petroleum.</p>
<p>The Sinivit project, formerly known as Wild Dog, lies south of Rabaul in East New Britain province.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
